<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mongolian People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mongolian People's Revolutionary Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mongolian People's Party is a political party founded in 1920 by Mongolian revolutionaries, among them Damdin Sükhbaatar. With the help of the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulaanbaatar">Urga</a> in 1921 and set up a government that became the Mongolian People's Republic in 1924. Renamed the Mongolian People's Revolutionary Party in 1925, it ruled as the sole party until 1990 and readopted its original name in 2010.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mongolian-peoples-party.jpg" alt="Mongolian People's Party" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Монгол Ардын Нам · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_Mongolian_People%27s_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
